      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CHURCHILLENA (8) appeals most with the upside at just her fourth start having improved nicely to this trip at Geelong last start, battling on well for second. With any further improvement she looks the one to beat. BALDONI (1) wasn't far behind CHURCHILLENA at Geelong last time out in third. That was his first go at this trip which is encouraging and he should take some beating again. WOLVES' DEN (7) has had a few chances this time in but is racing well, up to 2069m here last time and sticking on for third. Should be okay at the longer trip and will take catching again. RAGHNALL (6) showed some improvement rising sharply in trip second up when well backed and can do better again here third up. BELFAST BOY (2) is lightly raced and can improve.",
